  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After Ma tribe swallows Fei tribe at warm pond valley, elders congratulate the young man at the center for planning Fei internal discord so the ambush could take the valley. The text names him Ma tribe’s young tribe leader Ma Ying Jie: wide back, thin waist, sharp brows, bright eyes, rank four middle stage, enslavement path, and already called Little Ma Zun.",
      "chapters": [
        488
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_fei_tribe",
        "loc_warm_pond_valley",
        "fac_ma_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a wide back and thin waist, sharp brows and bright eyes, and a heroic spirit.",
      "chapters": [
        488
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He treats the valley as a defendable base of warm pools before the blizzard, points elders at Imperial Court blessed land and Eighty Eight True Yang Building, and borrows uncle Ma Zun’s prestige while fabricating praise in that uncle’s name.",
      "chapters": [
        489
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "warm-pond-valley-speech",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_imperial_court_blessed_land",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "char_ma_zun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later text states that after Fei tribe fell, Fei Cai was chosen as his personal servant.",
      "chapters": [
        520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "warm-pond-valley-speech",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fei_cai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Every guest who enters his tent must change shoes so the carpet stays clean, and the text calls him a clean freak. Fei Cai’s daily job is washing and replacing those shoes. When Fei Cai is framed for stealing the pair Ma Ying Jie usually wears, Ma Ying Jie nearly executes him, then accepts a silk wrap story because he is obsessed with cleanliness and would have been disgusted by shoes held bare against clothes. He then makes Fei Cai head of the slaves.",
      "chapters": [
        520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clean-freak-habits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mortals Fei Cai and Zhao Lian Yun find him injured on horseback after Ma tribe collapses. When he wakes, both nod that they saved him.",
      "chapters": [
        543
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rise-to-tribe-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_zhao_lian_yun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later renames Fei Cai as Fei Hong Yun after a new spirit spring is uncovered, then under Hei Lou Lan’s annexation pressure accepts outsiders into the Ma surname while planning to strip it later if the tribe recovers.",
      "chapters": [
        545
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rise-to-tribe-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ma_hong_yun",
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Eighty Eight True Yang Building he states he is an enslavement path master with no strength path affiliation, holding Ma Zun’s inheritance and the killer move Dragon Horse Spirit from a Snowy Mountain Gu Immortal.",
      "chapters": [
        579
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rise-to-tribe-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_dragon_horse_spirit",
        "loc_snowy_mountain",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the contest disaster the young tribe leader is luckily rescued, rises to tribe leader, and follows Hei tribe into Imperial Court blessed land when Hei Lou Lan forcibly annexes Ma tribe at warm pond valley.",
      "chapters": [
        588
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rise-to-tribe-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hei_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes Ma Ying Jie and Little Ma Zun. No Chinese characters for the personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
